{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfUSYpaDSRL1mssy8uiqA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do both — they're solving different problems, not competing for the same slot. But neither alone reliably hits the 6-month deadline: the hire's 3-month search plus onboarding ramp lands you a productive senior engineer around month 4-5 at best (and searches slip), while the training path's 8 weeks plus \"several more months\" of ramp likely lands past month 6 entirely. Training is really an attrition-resilience play (you're already losing ~2 of 7 people/year) rather than a fix for the committed feature.\n\nThe gap worth flagging: if you want real confidence in the 6-month commitment, you probably need a bridge for the delivery itself — a contractor/consultant with Kafka/Flink depth, or borrowing capacity from elsewhere — while the hire and the two internal trainees build durable capability in parallel. Want me to actually run the numbers/timeline on that (a proper first-principles pass), or is this enough to act on?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16589,"cache_read_input_tokens":24048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16589},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93589b1e-9525-4309-ae09-6afe42b18c7d","uuid":"6e652a0e-6159-4f4a-a218-285917afcc9d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:46:50.100Z","request_id":"req_011CfUSYpAAD4PZWbiPuT4oP"}
